# Template for `.dev.vars` — copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in real values (that file is gitignored).
# These are the SECRET values, injected for `wrangler dev` locally and via
# `wrangler secret put <NAME>` in production. Non-secret config lives in wrangler.jsonc `vars`.

# Nexudus API auth (NOT the account password). Generate the tokens from a
# username + password with `scripts/nexudus-token.sh`. These three are the seed:
# the Worker uses the access token, and on expiry refreshes with the refresh
# token (client_id = NEXUDUS_USERNAME) and keeps the rotating pair in KV.
NEXUDUS_USERNAME="service-account@example.com"  # account email, used as client_id on refresh
NEXUDUS_ACCESS_TOKEN="change-me"
NEXUDUS_REFRESH_TOKEN="change-me"

# Slack app credentials (Basic Information → Signing Secret; OAuth & Permissions
# → Bot User OAuth Token). Used to verify inbound requests and to open the modal
# / DM the result. See README.md (Slack app setup) for the app-setup steps.
SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET="change-me"
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN="xoxb-change-me"
